"""Geometry traced off r3tards/GyjP2nSXcAIz-VS.jpeg (the r3tards face: two sleepy eyes over a pair of brown lips, a thick
black line, on purple), in the reference's own pixels (1080 x 1080). r3tards.py maps it into the pet's 200 x 230 view.

The picture's ink is one connected shape. It was thinned to its centrelines (after the two irises, the black half discs
hanging from the upper lids, were taken out of it) and walked from junction to junction: STROKES are the fifteen lines,
each a list of (x, y, half-width) samples every 3 px, half-widths from a distance transform, so a line swells and thins
where the reference's does. PATCHES are the three crooks where lines meet that bands alone leave open. Drawn back as
bands they cover the reference's ink to within 2 px (97%; the rest is the 1 px fringe either way).

EYES (the left one first): "iris" is the black half disc, run on up under the lid to the lid's centre (so it can move
without showing its flat top; "irisshown" is the part the reference shows); "opening" is the white and the iris together,
grown 5 px so it tucks under the lines round it; "lidclip" is the opening plus the upper lid's own band (where the moving
lid line may show); "glints" are the white almond and dot on the iris, "heart" the pink heart. BROWN is the lips' fill,
grown under the lines. The tracer lived in the session scratchpad; this file is its output. Re-trace only if the
reference changes.
"""
